WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.063
Join selection becomes easier when you translate the
business question into a

00:00:04.076 --> 00:00:09.736
preservation rule If the question is only about
patients who have admissions

00:00:09.986 --> 00:00:15.623
requiring a match is appropriate so INNER JOIN fits
If the question

00:00:15.649 --> 00:00:19.689
says every patient whether or not an admission
exists then the patient

00:00:19.702 --> 00:00:24.455
population must be preserved Put patients on the
left and use LEFT

00:00:24.481 --> 00:00:30.238
JOIN If the question says every department including
empty departments

00:00:30.382 --> 00:00:34.530
preserve departments You can do that with RIGHT JOIN
as written in

00:00:34.556 --> 00:00:38.411
the earlier example or more commonly by moving
departments to the left

00:00:38.424 --> 00:00:43.108
and using LEFT JOIN If you need to compare two
sources and

00:00:43.134 --> 00:00:46.871
see unmatched rows from both FULL OUTER JOIN is a
natural choice

00:00:48.626 --> 00:00:51.599
Notice that we are choosing the join from the words
every only

00:00:51.612 --> 00:00:56.365
matched and unmatched from both sides That is much
more reliable than

00:00:56.378 --> 00:00:59.260
choosing a join because it is the one you remember
best
